// Routine moves away from a fight, told by the game itself (the host, 2026-10-21: "the lowest possible cost per turn"):
// a rest, a healing draught, a journey back to a place already visited, a search of the fallen, an order to a
// companion, the shield slung or taken up. The cards in the feed already show what the rules did; a request to the
// Dungeon Master only to say so again cost as much as a turn. `routineCalmTurn` decides whether a calm move needs the
// Dungeon Master (anything new, anyone who could react, anything with story weight goes to it); `calmTelling` writes
// the telling in the narrator's voice. fightLines.js `routineTelling` asks it for every move made out of a fight, so a
// device (useDmTurn.js) and the campaign server (server-turn.cjs) agree without a change of their own. Everything is
// seeded from the turn. Lines describe, never count: no numbers, no rule words.

// ---------- The line book ----------
// {place}/{Place}: where the journey ends; {name}: a companion; {hero}: the acting hero, in the twin after '|' that a
// table of several heroes reads (the hero by name, they/their after, never a guessed gender), as in fightLines.js.
